cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CLPS Lunar Mission Browser"
abstract: >-
  A static web tool that compares Moon south-pole landing sites by how long the
  Sun is visible, how long Earth (with a Deep Space Network dish in view) is
  visible, and the longest night. Built for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026,
  Lunar Landing Site Navigator. Not an official NASA product.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Big Four"
repository-code: "https://github.com/stevenjc2009-byte/clps-lunar-browser"
url: "https://stevenjc2009-byte.github.io/clps-lunar-browser/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Moon
  - lunar south pole
  - landing site
  - illumination
  - Skyfield
  - NASA Space Apps Challenge
